/**
@mainpage nRF Wi-Fi low-level API

This API documentation describes the OS-agnostic, low-level API for the Nordic
Semiconductor nRF70 Series FullMAC Wi-Fi companion ICs.

The API lets host software configure the radio processor unit (RPU), exchange
management traffic with the firmware, and send or receive 802.11 frames without
going through a specific operating system port. In the
<a href="https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ncs-latest/page/nrf/index.html">
nRF Connect SDK</a>, the same sources are integrated with Zephyr as the
<a href="https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ncs-latest/page/nrf/drivers/wifi/index.html">
nRF Wi-Fi driver</a>. Use the Zephyr networking stack unless you are porting the
driver to another operating system.

@section nrf_wifi_api_overview API structure

The interface is split into shared and mode-specific parts:

- @ref nrf_wifi_api_common "Common API" for initialization, deinitialization,
  and helpers used in all operating modes.
- @ref nrf_wifi_api "Wi-Fi mode API" for Station mode and future MAC modes
  intended for normal product use.
- @ref nrf_wifi_api_radio_test "Radio Test mode API" for RF validation
  firmware.

Select the API group that matches the firmware image loaded on the device. The
common API must be used together with exactly one of the mode-specific groups.

@section nrf_wifi_api_sources Source layout

Header files are located under the ``fw_if/umac_if/inc/`` folder, with
mode-specific subfolders.
Hardware abstraction and bus access are located under the :file:`hw_if/` and
:file:`os_if/` directories.
The Zephyr-specific driver that wraps this library is located in the
:file:`zephyr/drivers/wifi/nrf_wifi/` tree of the nRF Connect SDK.

@section nrf_wifi_api_ncs More documentation

For more information about product documentation, Kconfig options, samples, and
driver architecture, see the
<a href="https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ncs-latest/page/nrf/drivers/wifi/index.html">
nRF Connect SDK Wi-Fi documentation</a>.

*/
